---
source: kcl-lib/src/simulation_tests.rs
description: Result of unparsing named_views_duplicate_across_modules.kcl
---
// Pins that view names are unique per DECLARING module rather than per program.
// This file and the module it imports each declare a view named "Front", and
// both are accepted: a rule that compared names alone, without the module that
// declared them, would reject this program.
//
// The unit tests in execution::named_views pin the rule against module ids
// supplied directly. This test is what pins the wiring that supplies them, so a
// registration reading the wrong module id fails here rather than reaching an
// author. Importing the view value also has to leave the imported view
// registered to its own module, not re-registered to this one.
@settings(experimentalFeatures = allow)

import panelFront from "panel.kcl"

localFront = view::named("Front", camera = view::oriented(view::Orientation::Back), baseline = view::Visibility::Show)

importedFront = panelFront
